From 3e84ff14b56c8bb4fd43f91cf5e6a5fd0cfad9ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ry <noreply@local>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:47:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Nebulos embedding (RECONSTRUCTED 2026-11-08 after loss of
 the original fork)

Base: upstream azahar-emu/azahar 6b4e7f2e6 (tag 2127.0-rc2 + 0). The original base commit and
patches were lost; everything below is re-created from the decompiled Nebulos Release 15 APK
(Java side) and from the exports/strings of its libcitra-android.so (native side). Anything not
marked "RECONSTRUCTED" is upstream.

Build:
- :app is an Android library (AGP 9.2.1, Kotlin 2.4.0 via buildscript classpath, safeargs 2.9.6),
  arm64-v8a only, no applicationId/signing/ktlint/validation-layer download.
  BuildConfig.VERSION_NAME defined by hand (libraries have none).
- res/drawable/scrollbar_thumb.xml: remove stray duplicated xml declaration (AGP 9 aapt parse fails).

Java/Kotlin (RECONSTRUCTED hooks):
- utils/NebulosBridge, utils/NebulosToast: notice/error/ready/progress/loadingText seam (same
  shape as the Eden port); fatal parking.
- CitraApplication.initializeForEmbedding(Application) + host context.
- NativeLibrary: onCoreError/displayAlertMsg routed to NebulosBridge (no dialogs); new externals
  setSaveDirectories, setFourThreeFill, setFramePatch, isEmulationFinished.
- EmulationFragment: shader progress/loading text/ready -> NebulosBridge; toasts -> NebulosToast.
  EmulationActivity/SoftwareKeyboard/TurboHelper/NetPlayManager/GamepadEventHandler: no dialogs/toasts.
- file:// user directory support (PermissionsHandler.hasWriteAccess/userRootDocument, SettingsFile,
  GpuDriverHelper, FileUtil.createFile/createDir).
- IntSetting.int / BooleanSetting.boolean / SettingsFile.saveFile compat shims over CitraSettings
  (the host was written against the older enum-field settings API).
- InputOverlay.NEBULOS_NO_OVERLAY marker.

Native (RECONSTRUCTED, guessed from symbols/log strings of the old library):
- FileUtil::SetSaveDirectoryOverrides + JNI setSaveDirectories (portable sdmc/nand/states; Android
  paths are "!"-prefixed absolute paths).
- JNI isEmulationFinished (set after System::Shutdown), setFramePatch (per-slice guest memory patch
  enforcement, verification of original words, once-words on turn-off).
- JNI setFourThreeFill: flag only. NOT RECOVERED: the renderer-side 4:3 fill (vertex-shader hud_adj)
  and the draw blending ("interp") half of the 60 fps patch, plus the svcprof debug profiler.

